From: xucy10 <someonm20141923@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Guard Connection.flush() against null channel

Leaves fakeplayer (bot) connections use BotConnection with a null channel
and no real network. Any queued Connection::flush action drained by
processQueue() would dereference this.channel.eventLoop() and crash the
region with an NPE on every bot login. Add a null guard directly in
flush() so every entry point (flushChannel, tickChildren resumeFlushing,
future callers) is safe for channelless connections.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
index 6b85a5a..53247b8 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
@@ -530,6 +530,7 @@ public class Connection extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet<?>> {
     }
 
     private void flush() {
+        if (this.channel == null) return; // Mili - fakeplayer connections have no real channel; draining queued actions must not NPE
         if (this.channel.eventLoop().inEventLoop()) {
             this.channel.flush();
         } else {
